                        "entry_id": "c9229f38-ceae-3949-bfee-5a897beabf2a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Militant; warlike."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f2faa85-0265-4f07-9a0a-a96964d322e6",
                                "sense_id": "4fc55264-5fa2-3725-a84b-9d2191ccba8d",
                                "text": "Brightned the black horizon of his parish ; Gave to the Prince of Darkness such hard blows, That Satan was afraid to show his nose, (Except in hell), before this priest so warrish!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88a6c067-cd28-46dc-ba45-c559091e7d23",
                                "sense_id": "4fc55264-5fa2-3725-a84b-9d2191ccba8d",
                                "text": "Dear George, 'tis very true,\" replied the king, \" Poor Honour is just come upon the parish; Merit may tramp tho streets, and ballads sing: My new-made knights can boast of nothing warrish."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bfbbebca-fb63-460f-8946-00bde25ebf4d",
                                "sense_id": "4fc55264-5fa2-3725-a84b-9d2191ccba8d",
                                "text": "The specific examples of warrish attitudes change from year to year, but the underlying bellicosity remains."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c4f1a6b-d9fa-4e43-8027-5a2ab079c483",
                                "sense_id": "4fc55264-5fa2-3725-a84b-9d2191ccba8d",
                                "text": "Some of the soldiers were little more than boys; they had spent their entire lives practicing their caste's warrish obligations, but they had never marched to battle for their king. Nevertheless, they understood the War Rites; […]"
                            }
                        ]
